Body:
I validated a practical compatibility strategy downstream and suggest this upstream shape for the real fix:

1. Replace broad substring skip with exact package-id skip only.
2. Emit a warning when skipping a configured plugin entry.
3. Add explicit opt-in override env for external plugin loading.

Pseudo-patch in `packages/opencode/src/plugin/index.ts`:

```ts
const blocked = new Set(["opencode-openai-codex-auth", "opencode-copilot-auth"])
const allowLegacy = process.env.OPENCODE_ALLOW_LEGACY_PLUGIN === "1"

function packageId(entry: string) {
  if (entry.startsWith("file://")) return null
  const at = entry.lastIndexOf("@")
  return at > 0 ? entry.slice(0, at) : entry
}

for (let plugin of plugins) {
  const id = packageId(plugin)
  if (!allowLegacy && id && blocked.has(id)) {
    log.warn("skipping blocked plugin", { plugin, reason: "supported first-party" })
    continue
  }
  // existing load/install path
}
```

This avoids false positives for `file://` paths and makes behavior observable for users.

Could we add adding agents like we can add skills by adding path?

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "skills": {
    "paths": ["./node_modules/<my_skills_package>/skills/"]
  },
}
```

Something like this:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "agents": {
    "paths": ["./node_modules/<my_skills_package>/agents/"]
  },
}
```

Closing as duplicate of [1.0.2 - Themes in opencode.json files not respected. #3634
](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/3634)

> **NOTE**: This is about tui.json (the recommended config location per docs), while #3634 was about opencode.json. If the fix differs for tui.json, please let me know - happy to help test.

